rmanmaurer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-04-29T16:57:25Z","updated_at":"2013-04-29T16:57:25Z","body":"We always notify the promise before fire the event. This is needed to keep it consistent and also to be sure the promise is already set as it may be used within the event method of a handler too .\n\nAm 29.04.2013 um 17:49 schrieb Jeff Pinner notifications@github.com:\n\n> I had an error where fireChannelRegistered throws an exception (initHeadHandler failed) but then I got this exception:\n> \n> java.lang.IllegalStateException: complete already\n> at io.netty.util.concurrent.DefaultPromise.setFailure(DefaultPromise.java:385)\n> at io.netty.channel.DefaultChannelPromise.setFailure(DefaultChannelPromise.java:86)\n> at io.netty.channel.AbstractChannel$AbstractUnsafe.register0(AbstractChannel.java:623)\n> \n> I think promise.setSuccess should be moved until after fireChannelActive()\n> \n> —\n> Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/17179317/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"normanmaurer","id":439362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/439362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer","html_url":"https://github.com/normanmaurer",